1
00:00:25,893 --> 00:00:28,126
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,303
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:51,450
♪ ♪

4
00:01:20,014 --> 00:01:21,980
♪ ♪

5
00:01:42,469 --> 00:01:44,403
♪ ♪

6
00:02:06,493 --> 00:02:09,594
Three days...

7
00:02:09,662 --> 00:02:14,299
after this defendant took
the sacred vows of marriage

8
00:02:14,368 --> 00:02:18,203
with Ann Wilson, Hmm.

9
00:02:18,272 --> 00:02:22,874
He purchased a $1,000,000
life insurance policy

10
00:02:22,943 --> 00:02:25,977
on his new wife's life.

11
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:32,083
The months went by.

12
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:35,420
One, two, three.

13
00:02:35,488 --> 00:02:39,157
And then... Then,
ladies and gentlemen,

14
00:02:39,226 --> 00:02:42,660
Ann Wilson disappeared
off the face of this earth.

15
00:02:42,729 --> 00:02:47,365
She disappeared because

16
00:02:47,434 --> 00:02:51,303
this defendant Kenneth
Wilson, her husband,

17
00:02:51,372 --> 00:02:54,406
took her life away.

18
00:02:54,475 --> 00:02:57,309
Huh.

19
00:02:57,378 --> 00:02:59,678
A perfect crime.

20
00:02:59,747 --> 00:03:01,279
Almost.

21
00:03:01,348 --> 00:03:06,651
Tiny blood stains on
that blue bathroom towel.

22
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:08,620
And tiny blood stains

23
00:03:08,689 --> 00:03:11,089
in the trunk of his car.

24
00:03:11,158 --> 00:03:13,291
Both Ann Wilson's blood type.

25
00:03:15,962 --> 00:03:21,500
Now, you can never bring
Ann Wilson back again.

26
00:03:22,669 --> 00:03:25,003
No.

27
00:03:25,071 --> 00:03:29,807
But you can and you
must find her killer

28
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:35,613
guilty of murder
in the first degree.

29
00:03:35,682 --> 00:03:37,616
Thank you.

30
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:50,762
People of the State of
Georgia v. Kenneth Wilson.

31
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:56,668
You believe that,
ladies and gentlemen?

32
00:03:56,737 --> 00:04:00,606
Thousands of
county and city police,

33
00:04:00,674 --> 00:04:05,176
millions of dollars in
resources and bureaucracy,

34
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:10,082
and the prosecution
does not have a fingerprint,

35
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:14,886
a murder weapon, a witness.

36
00:04:14,955 --> 00:04:18,156
They have not been
able to show us the body

37
00:04:18,225 --> 00:04:22,627
of Ann Wilson to prove
beyond a reasonable doubt

38
00:04:22,696 --> 00:04:26,097
that anyone took her life,

39
00:04:26,166 --> 00:04:28,533
much less Kenneth Wilson.

40
00:04:32,372 --> 00:04:34,606
Kenneth Wilson loved his wife.

41
00:04:36,944 --> 00:04:44,849
He feels nothing
but grief at her loss.

42
00:04:44,918 --> 00:04:47,752
He committed no crime,
perfect or otherwise.

43
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:53,891
You must understand his tragedy,

44
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:57,962
and his loss is his tragedy.

45
00:04:58,031 --> 00:05:00,898
<i>We find the defendant guilty.</i>

46
00:05:41,474 --> 00:05:43,508
Hi. Are you the manager?

47
00:05:43,576 --> 00:05:45,343
We're filled up.
Nothing for rent.

48
00:05:45,412 --> 00:05:48,213
No... Does Norman
Bauer still live here?

49
00:05:48,282 --> 00:05:49,547
Not anymore.

50
00:05:49,616 --> 00:05:51,149
Well, he moved?

51
00:05:51,218 --> 00:05:52,650
He died.

52
00:05:52,719 --> 00:05:54,852
When?

53
00:05:54,922 --> 00:05:57,923
A few days ago. A
heart attack or something.

54
00:05:57,991 --> 00:06:01,159
Everything. Cancer.
Smoked all the time.

55
00:06:01,228 --> 00:06:02,760
Who came and got his things?

56
00:06:02,829 --> 00:06:05,196
Nobody yet.

57
00:06:05,265 --> 00:06:08,666
Uh, well, I had to
sell some of his stuff.

58
00:06:08,735 --> 00:06:11,002
Pay the rent and utilities.

59
00:06:11,071 --> 00:06:12,337
The rest is in the basement.

60
00:06:12,406 --> 00:06:14,539
Look, I was his brother-in-law.

61
00:06:14,607 --> 00:06:16,807
Um, I'd be happy to
clear his things out for you.

62
00:06:19,112 --> 00:06:20,211
Fine.

63
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:23,014
50 buck storage
fee and it's yours.

64
00:06:25,151 --> 00:06:28,052
<i>I can't help it, Ben,</i>
I love her! Who?

65
00:06:28,121 --> 00:06:29,587
Bernice Wooley.

66
00:06:29,656 --> 00:06:31,589
She's the love of my life.

67
00:06:31,658 --> 00:06:33,925
Where did you meet
her? Templin's Bar.

68
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:37,329
Gorgeous brunette.

69
00:06:37,397 --> 00:06:38,607
Big eyes.

70
00:06:38,631 --> 00:06:39,675
Full lips.

71
00:06:39,699 --> 00:06:40,731
How old is she?

72
00:06:40,801 --> 00:06:41,944
Uh, 48-ish.

73
00:06:41,968 --> 00:06:42,968
Oh!

74
00:06:44,137 --> 00:06:45,782
And it's not just physical.

75
00:06:45,806 --> 00:06:47,539
No, she's smart, too.

76
00:06:47,608 --> 00:06:51,042
She does crossword
puzzles in ink.

77
00:06:51,111 --> 00:06:54,212
And she knows all the words
to "Hard-Hearted Hannah."

78
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:58,116
At least that's
what she told me.

79
00:06:59,352 --> 00:07:02,320
"Hard-Hearted Hannah,
Vamp of Savannah."

80
00:07:02,389 --> 00:07:03,599
She's got a birthday coming up.

81
00:07:03,623 --> 00:07:05,168
What do you think
I ought to get her?

82
00:07:05,192 --> 00:07:06,357
Oh, I don't know.

83
00:07:06,426 --> 00:07:08,459
Ladies like flowers or candy.

84
00:07:08,528 --> 00:07:10,895
Too square.

85
00:07:10,964 --> 00:07:12,864
Hmm.

86
00:07:18,205 --> 00:07:19,437
Well, Ken!

87
00:07:19,506 --> 00:07:20,872
Come in!

88
00:07:20,941 --> 00:07:23,486
Ben, I've discovered
something you won't believe.

89
00:07:23,510 --> 00:07:24,642
Yeah?

90
00:07:24,711 --> 00:07:26,844
I heard you had been paroled.

91
00:07:26,914 --> 00:07:29,647
Hey, Les, this is Ken Wilson.
My neighbor Les Calhoun.

92
00:07:29,716 --> 00:07:31,616
Hey. Hey.

93
00:07:31,685 --> 00:07:32,829
Hey. How do you do?

94
00:07:32,853 --> 00:07:34,397
Now what was that
you were saying?

95
00:07:34,421 --> 00:07:36,332
Do you remember
Norman Bauer? Uh...

96
00:07:36,356 --> 00:07:37,622
He was my brother-in-law.

97
00:07:37,691 --> 00:07:39,535
He was stationed in Greece
when my wife disappeared.

98
00:07:39,559 --> 00:07:40,792
Oh, yeah.

99
00:07:40,861 --> 00:07:42,672
Well, I tracked him down
to Atlanta. Is that right?

100
00:07:42,696 --> 00:07:43,795
He's dead.

101
00:07:43,864 --> 00:07:45,464
Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.

102
00:07:45,532 --> 00:07:50,335
Ben, I have spent the last
seven years sitting in a jail cell.

103
00:07:50,404 --> 00:07:52,970
Thinking about Ann
and nothing else.

104
00:07:53,039 --> 00:07:55,106
I know and I'm sorry

105
00:07:55,175 --> 00:07:56,335
I couldn't do more for you.

106
00:07:56,376 --> 00:07:57,687
Nobody could have
done more for me.

107
00:07:57,711 --> 00:07:59,188
You didn't have
anything to go on.

108
00:07:59,212 --> 00:08:01,045
But I found something.

109
00:08:01,114 --> 00:08:02,513
I found these in Norman Bauer's

110
00:08:02,582 --> 00:08:04,282
personal effects.

111
00:08:04,350 --> 00:08:06,685
They're cancelled
checks. Eight of them.

112
00:08:06,753 --> 00:08:09,420
Each one of them is
made out for $100,000,

113
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:12,523
all of them payable to Golden
West Land Management.

114
00:08:12,592 --> 00:08:15,126
Two checks a year
for the past four years.

115
00:08:15,195 --> 00:08:18,362
Every one of those is endorsed
by somebody named Kelly Manning.

116
00:08:18,431 --> 00:08:20,610
That's right, that's right.

117
00:08:20,634 --> 00:08:23,112
Norman inherited all
that insurance money.

118
00:08:23,136 --> 00:08:24,413
A million dollars.

119
00:08:24,437 --> 00:08:25,548
Yeah, but you should have seen

120
00:08:25,572 --> 00:08:27,316
the boarding house
he was living in.

121
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:28,740
It was a dump.

122
00:08:28,809 --> 00:08:32,410
Well, if there was an
insurance policy on Ken's wife,

123
00:08:32,479 --> 00:08:34,290
why did her brother
get all the money?

124
00:08:34,314 --> 00:08:36,947
Because I was in
prison for Ann's murder.

125
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:39,817
Law says a criminal
can't profit by his crime.

126
00:08:39,886 --> 00:08:42,053
Oh, that makes sense.

127
00:08:42,122 --> 00:08:43,521
As I remember it,

128
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:45,790
the insurance policy
was Ann's idea, wasn't it?

129
00:08:45,826 --> 00:08:47,057
Yes.

130
00:08:47,127 --> 00:08:51,630
He brother inherits
all this money,

131
00:08:51,698 --> 00:08:55,533
invests in some real
estate company in California,

132
00:08:55,602 --> 00:08:57,636
and yet, he lives like a pauper.

133
00:08:57,704 --> 00:09:00,639
Oh, Ben, you got
to get right on this

134
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:03,207
and this Kelly Manning
fella... That's your key.

135
00:09:03,276 --> 00:09:08,179
Um, I-I-I wouldn't get
my hopes up too high,

136
00:09:08,248 --> 00:09:09,926
but you're right. You're right.

137
00:09:09,950 --> 00:09:12,150
This is something to go on.

138
00:09:21,728 --> 00:09:24,395
Hi. Um, I'm here to
see Kelly Manning.

139
00:09:24,464 --> 00:09:27,164
I'm Ken Wilson, but I
don't have an appointment.

140
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:33,872
Yes?

141
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:36,780
There's a Ken Wilson
here to see you.

142
00:09:42,649 --> 00:09:43,959
She'll be with you
in just a minute.

143
00:09:43,983 --> 00:09:45,917
Kelly Manning's a woman?

144
00:09:45,985 --> 00:09:48,019
Definitely.

145
00:10:06,506 --> 00:10:07,672
Mr. Wilson?

146
00:10:14,647 --> 00:10:16,514
Ann?

147
00:10:16,582 --> 00:10:18,449
I'm Kelly Manning.

148
00:10:18,518 --> 00:10:19,717
You wanted to see me?

149
00:10:21,688 --> 00:10:23,554
Mr. Wilson?

150
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,657
I'm sorry. You...

151
00:10:25,725 --> 00:10:28,025
You remind me of
someone. I'm sorry.

152
00:10:28,094 --> 00:10:30,394
Oh, that's all right.

153
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:31,896
What can I do for you?

154
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:34,232
Uh, Norman Bauer.
We were related.

155
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,534
He sent you a lot of
money over the years

156
00:10:36,603 --> 00:10:39,670
and I wondered why.

157
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:42,039
Oh, Mr. Bauer is
one of our investors.

158
00:10:42,108 --> 00:10:43,908
He died.

159
00:10:46,013 --> 00:10:47,112
When did he die?

160
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:48,412
Just-Just recently.

161
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:50,982
Oh, I'm sorry.

162
00:10:51,051 --> 00:10:52,316
Are you an accountant?

163
00:10:52,385 --> 00:10:54,018
No. No, I'm not.

164
00:10:54,087 --> 00:10:55,431
Well, uh...

165
00:10:55,455 --> 00:10:57,399
If you'll excuse me,
Mr. Wilson, I really must get...

166
00:10:57,423 --> 00:10:58,522
Wait, wait, wait.

167
00:10:58,591 --> 00:11:00,825
Please. You look
so much like Ann.

168
00:11:00,893 --> 00:11:03,594
Please, Mr. Wilson.

169
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:04,796
What's going on here?

170
00:11:04,864 --> 00:11:07,598
Mr. Wilson seems to
have made a mistake.

171
00:11:07,667 --> 00:11:10,227
That's all. Haven't
you, Mr. Wilson?

172
00:11:11,504 --> 00:11:13,437
I'm sorry.

173
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:33,484
Hello, Kelly!

174
00:13:02,148 --> 00:13:03,982
♪ ♪

175
00:13:32,745 --> 00:13:34,712
♪ ♪

176
00:14:03,409 --> 00:14:05,042
♪ ♪

177
00:14:34,007 --> 00:14:35,807
♪ ♪

178
00:14:51,257 --> 00:14:54,124
Absolutely, it's
a terrific deal.

179
00:14:54,193 --> 00:14:56,827
You'll love your new
weekend home at Sun Springs.

180
00:14:56,896 --> 00:15:01,565
The entertaining you'll
do? Don't forget to invite me.

181
00:15:01,635 --> 00:15:03,534
Ask any banker, any
investment counselor,

182
00:15:03,603 --> 00:15:05,970
anybody that knows
anything at all about money,

183
00:15:06,039 --> 00:15:08,205
and they'll all tell
you the same thing:

184
00:15:08,274 --> 00:15:09,640
real estate.

185
00:15:09,709 --> 00:15:11,487
Do you carry the
financing yourselves?

186
00:15:11,511 --> 00:15:13,978
Great crowd.

187
00:15:14,047 --> 00:15:16,258
Mm. Didn't imagine
it would go so well.

188
00:15:16,282 --> 00:15:19,149
Listen, I better
go. See you later.

189
00:15:19,218 --> 00:15:20,938
Okay, sounds good.

190
00:15:22,722 --> 00:15:24,422
Ann, how could you do that?

191
00:15:24,490 --> 00:15:27,992
Mr. Wilson, I already told
you, you made a mistake.

192
00:15:28,061 --> 00:15:29,160
What about this?

193
00:15:31,063 --> 00:15:32,629
You broke into my house?

194
00:15:32,698 --> 00:15:34,198
Okay, pal,

195
00:15:34,267 --> 00:15:36,746
what's with you? I gave this
to you as a wedding present.

196
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:38,002
He is crazy.

197
00:15:38,071 --> 00:15:40,015
You sent me to prison for a
crime that never happened.

198
00:15:40,039 --> 00:15:41,117
How could you do that?

199
00:15:41,141 --> 00:15:43,218
Just so you could
collect a million bucks?

200
00:15:43,242 --> 00:15:44,575
Okay, okay, okay.

201
00:15:44,643 --> 00:15:47,189
Ann, why? This guy's a
nut. Get him out of here.

202
00:15:47,213 --> 00:15:49,191
I don't understand why.
We loved each other.

203
00:15:49,215 --> 00:15:51,575
Come on! Come on!
We were married! Why?!

204
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,759
What's going on here?

205
00:16:01,828 --> 00:16:06,397
Hey, the guy's crazy.
What can I say?

206
00:16:10,870 --> 00:16:13,604
Here, kitty-kitty-kitty-kitty!

207
00:16:37,963 --> 00:16:41,098
Kelly? Are you all right?

208
00:16:47,574 --> 00:16:48,672
Kelly?

209
00:16:52,178 --> 00:16:53,711
Kelly?

210
00:17:03,589 --> 00:17:05,189
Uh...

211
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:09,993
Oh!

212
00:17:12,298 --> 00:17:13,897
Help!

213
00:17:28,781 --> 00:17:32,617
Are you gonna play? I
might as well play with the cat.

214
00:17:32,685 --> 00:17:35,620
Oh, it's just that other
guys are chasing Bernice.

215
00:17:35,688 --> 00:17:36,787
Oh.

216
00:17:36,856 --> 00:17:40,758
Chester Taft took her
bowling the other night.

217
00:17:40,826 --> 00:17:43,894
Oh. I-I don't think I know him.

218
00:17:43,963 --> 00:17:45,907
Oh, he wears his
hair in a pompadour

219
00:17:45,931 --> 00:17:47,365
and thinks he's Don Ameche.

220
00:17:47,433 --> 00:17:49,133
Mm.

221
00:17:49,201 --> 00:17:50,901
Anyway, I finally found

222
00:17:50,970 --> 00:17:52,681
the perfect birthday
gift for Bernice,

223
00:17:52,705 --> 00:17:55,473
and I have to send away,
and it won't get here in time.

224
00:17:55,541 --> 00:18:00,456
Well, that's... Hello.

225
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:03,781
You're kidding?

226
00:18:03,850 --> 00:18:06,984
No. No, no,
listen, listen, listen.

227
00:18:07,053 --> 00:18:10,288
Don't say anything to anybody.

228
00:18:10,356 --> 00:18:12,123
I'm on my way.

229
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,860
Who was that?

230
00:18:15,929 --> 00:18:20,464
Ken Wilson's just been
arrested for killing his wife.

231
00:18:20,533 --> 00:18:21,533
Again?

232
00:18:29,408 --> 00:18:32,276
<i>The fact is that a person
in the state of California</i>

233
00:18:32,345 --> 00:18:35,679
<i>is dead, the victim of a
violent and brutal murder.</i>

234
00:18:35,748 --> 00:18:37,248
But it's unconstitutional!

235
00:18:37,317 --> 00:18:40,384
My client has already
paid the penalty

236
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:41,718
for this crime in full!

237
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:43,565
He paid the penalty for
that crime, Mr. Matlock,

238
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:44,655
not for this one.

239
00:18:44,723 --> 00:18:46,301
This is not a
constitutional issue here.

240
00:18:46,325 --> 00:18:48,270
Are-are you saying
we should just forget

241
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:50,272
about the seven
years he spent in prison

242
00:18:50,296 --> 00:18:52,307
for this very same crime
he's now accused of?

243
00:18:52,331 --> 00:18:53,697
What are you
suggesting, counselor?

244
00:18:53,766 --> 00:18:55,432
He paid for the
penalty for this crime

245
00:18:55,501 --> 00:18:57,268
in advance? That's outrageous!

246
00:18:57,336 --> 00:18:59,503
I'm suggesting... Thank
you, thank you, counsel.

247
00:18:59,572 --> 00:19:00,972
I've heard enough.

248
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:03,586
This court specifically
finds that the defendant

249
00:19:03,610 --> 00:19:05,220
would not be facing
double jeopardy.

250
00:19:05,244 --> 00:19:08,112
Therefore, defense
motion to dismiss is denied.

251
00:19:08,181 --> 00:19:09,525
The trial date remains the same.

252
00:19:09,549 --> 00:19:11,460
I look forward to seeing
you next week, counsel.

253
00:19:11,484 --> 00:19:12,764
The court's adjourned.

254
00:19:21,393 --> 00:19:23,994
Ben Matlock, this is Bob
King and Steve Davidson.

255
00:19:24,063 --> 00:19:25,174
Mr. Matlock.

256
00:19:25,198 --> 00:19:26,875
Oh, well, this is an
unexpected pleasure.

257
00:19:26,899 --> 00:19:30,000
I thought my meeting
was just with Mr. Davidson.

258
00:19:30,069 --> 00:19:33,070
Well, I have to be at Sun
Springs in less than two hours.

259
00:19:33,139 --> 00:19:34,483
Mm. Please, sit down.

260
00:19:34,507 --> 00:19:36,974
Oh.

261
00:19:37,043 --> 00:19:41,479
Mr. Matlock, these
are real Havanas.

262
00:19:41,548 --> 00:19:42,813
May I offer you a smoke?

263
00:19:42,882 --> 00:19:46,250
No, I, uh, I, uh, the
only smoke I like

264
00:19:46,319 --> 00:19:49,453
is in a fireplace
or under a nice

265
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:50,522
shoulder of pork.

266
00:19:51,591 --> 00:19:53,168
What can we do
for you, Mr. Matlock?

267
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:54,358
Please, sit down.

268
00:19:54,427 --> 00:19:58,162
Uh, thanks. Well,
you have me curious.

269
00:19:58,230 --> 00:20:02,433
I-I just was wondering why
two honest businessman

270
00:20:02,501 --> 00:20:04,568
like yourself would get involved

271
00:20:04,636 --> 00:20:06,515
with a con artist
like Kelly Manning.

272
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:09,206
We got conned.

273
00:20:09,275 --> 00:20:11,942
She presented herself as
a hard-working young lady

274
00:20:12,011 --> 00:20:14,022
that wanted to learn
the real estate business

275
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:15,980
and we bought it.

276
00:20:16,049 --> 00:20:19,417
Oh. The way I hear it, you
gave her a full partnership

277
00:20:19,485 --> 00:20:22,186
the day after she
walked through the door.

278
00:20:22,254 --> 00:20:23,620
Uh...

279
00:20:23,689 --> 00:20:29,226
Let me explain. Kelly Manning
bought her way into this company

280
00:20:29,295 --> 00:20:34,398
with $400,000. Made
her very welcome.

281
00:20:34,467 --> 00:20:36,867
We didn't know she obtained
this money through fraud.

282
00:20:36,936 --> 00:20:38,803
Oh.

283
00:20:38,871 --> 00:20:42,939
Uh, well, I-I don't suppose
either one of you killed her?

284
00:20:45,845 --> 00:20:48,405
I mean, you both had alibis?

285
00:20:48,747 --> 00:20:51,215
I was with one of our
sales representatives,

286
00:20:51,284 --> 00:20:56,453
Terri Young, till,
ooh, about 2:00 A.M.

287
00:20:56,522 --> 00:21:00,057
Oh... Oh, strictly
business, gentlemen!

288
00:21:00,126 --> 00:21:01,758
Mr. King?

289
00:21:01,827 --> 00:21:03,293
I was at home reading.

290
00:21:03,362 --> 00:21:04,362
By yourself?

291
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:06,930
Yes, by myself.

292
00:21:06,999 --> 00:21:09,500
I'm sorry. I think
I'm gonna be late.

293
00:21:09,569 --> 00:21:11,479
Oh. Well, I appreciate
your time. Certainly.

294
00:21:11,503 --> 00:21:13,971
Hey, if there's anything
else we can do for you.

295
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:15,550
Thank you. Thank you very much.

296
00:21:15,574 --> 00:21:17,614
Please. Mm-hmm.

297
00:21:58,284 --> 00:22:01,451
Sun Springs was made
for couples like you.

298
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:03,465
You're absolutely
gonna love it out here.

299
00:22:03,489 --> 00:22:06,356
What time would you like
me to meet you at the bank?

300
00:22:06,425 --> 00:22:10,761
Okay, see you then. Bye.

301
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:14,098
Hi. Can I help you?

302
00:22:14,167 --> 00:22:15,632
That's quite possible.

303
00:22:15,701 --> 00:22:18,769
Sun Springs looks like
a perfect investment.

304
00:22:18,838 --> 00:22:21,972
We expect our homes
to double in value.

305
00:22:22,041 --> 00:22:24,341
Now you're talking
my kind of numbers.

306
00:22:24,410 --> 00:22:26,121
Do you want to buy
one of our homes?

307
00:22:26,145 --> 00:22:29,579
One is light housekeeping.

308
00:22:29,649 --> 00:22:31,815
I'm talking investment here.

309
00:22:31,884 --> 00:22:33,483
Five, maybe six.

310
00:22:33,553 --> 00:22:35,553
Six?

311
00:22:35,621 --> 00:22:38,789
My only concern is that
my investment appreciate.

312
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:40,991
I need to know that
Sun Springs is going

313
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:43,104
to be a stable community.
Now, I have heard otherwise.

314
00:22:43,128 --> 00:22:45,107
There's this issue
of a Miss Manning.

315
00:22:45,131 --> 00:22:49,633
Now, please, be candid
with me, Miss Young.

316
00:22:49,702 --> 00:22:52,670
I am about to hand you
a fortune in commissions.

317
00:22:52,738 --> 00:22:54,905
Now, did Miss Manning
have an argument

318
00:22:54,973 --> 00:22:56,440
with her business partners?

319
00:22:56,509 --> 00:22:58,976
She did not.

320
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:01,712
And did you get
along well with her?

321
00:23:01,781 --> 00:23:05,382
That's rather a
personal question.

322
00:23:05,451 --> 00:23:07,952
But we didn't argue.

323
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:10,353
In fact, on the
night of her murder,

324
00:23:10,422 --> 00:23:14,257
I was with one of
the partners working.

325
00:23:14,326 --> 00:23:18,461
Thank you. I didn't
mean to get personal.

326
00:23:18,530 --> 00:23:19,729
You've been very nice.

327
00:23:19,799 --> 00:23:21,098
Bye-bye.

328
00:23:21,167 --> 00:23:25,369
Excuse me. Do you
have a business card?

329
00:23:25,438 --> 00:23:27,170
Of course.

330
00:23:34,179 --> 00:23:37,248
"Tyler Hudson."

331
00:23:37,316 --> 00:23:38,527
You're a private investigator?

332
00:23:39,719 --> 00:23:40,917
Get out of here!

333
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:09,046
You know, I really don't want
to talk about this right now.

334
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:10,814
I'm very upset.

335
00:24:13,986 --> 00:24:17,587
Were you a close
friend of Kelly Manning?

336
00:24:17,656 --> 00:24:20,523
Well, I wouldn't
exactly say that.

337
00:24:20,592 --> 00:24:23,961
It's hard to be close to someone
who has everything, you know...

338
00:24:24,029 --> 00:24:26,496
Brains, money, looks.

339
00:24:26,565 --> 00:24:28,765
Especially when they're
not too fond of company.

340
00:24:30,536 --> 00:24:32,436
But you called the police?

341
00:24:32,505 --> 00:24:35,405
Well-well, yeah, I found her.

342
00:24:35,475 --> 00:24:37,908
And you know, as soon as I
pushed open that front door,

343
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:40,277
I had the most awful feeling,

344
00:24:40,345 --> 00:24:42,190
because she used to
always keep it locked.

345
00:24:42,214 --> 00:24:44,614
She insisted on her privacy.

346
00:24:44,683 --> 00:24:46,050
But you came in?

347
00:24:46,118 --> 00:24:50,020
Well, yeah, I did come in.

348
00:24:50,089 --> 00:24:52,722
Well, did you see
anything or hear anything?

349
00:24:52,792 --> 00:24:55,959
Well, I-I, um, called
her name twice,

350
00:24:56,028 --> 00:24:59,863
because she didn't always
answer the first time, and...

351
00:24:59,932 --> 00:25:01,576
Did she answer this time?

352
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:04,067
No, no, but-but I
did hear something.

353
00:25:04,136 --> 00:25:06,370
Um, I can't describe it.

354
00:25:06,439 --> 00:25:11,275
It, um... well, it
sounded like, um...

355
00:25:11,344 --> 00:25:12,610
"beep-beep."

356
00:25:14,813 --> 00:25:17,648
"Beep-beep."

357
00:25:17,716 --> 00:25:20,651
Well, anyway, then
I heard somebody

358
00:25:20,720 --> 00:25:22,519
going out the back
door, you know,

359
00:25:22,588 --> 00:25:23,588
so I called out again

360
00:25:23,623 --> 00:25:25,188
and when I still
didn't get an answer,

361
00:25:25,257 --> 00:25:27,991
then I... went in there.

362
00:25:30,295 --> 00:25:32,863
And that's when I saw...

363
00:25:32,932 --> 00:25:35,199
poor Kelly lying there.

364
00:25:35,268 --> 00:25:37,968
Oh, the blood all over.

365
00:25:38,036 --> 00:25:41,004
Still beautiful, but...

366
00:25:41,073 --> 00:25:43,874
Oh, I'm-I'm...
just... I'm too upset.

367
00:25:43,942 --> 00:25:47,711
You have to
excuse... Oh, I'm sorry.

368
00:25:47,779 --> 00:25:49,780
I'm sorry.

369
00:25:54,053 --> 00:25:55,985
Hmm.

370
00:26:26,018 --> 00:26:28,697
<i>I told you I didn't
tell him anything.</i>

371
00:26:28,721 --> 00:26:30,899
How do I know you
didn't let something slip?

372
00:26:30,923 --> 00:26:32,589
'Cause I'm too smart to slip.

373
00:26:32,657 --> 00:26:34,725
I'm too smart not to know
when somebody owes me,

374
00:26:34,793 --> 00:26:37,060
and you owe me big...

375
00:26:37,129 --> 00:26:39,096
Maybe I should wait outside.

376
00:26:39,164 --> 00:26:41,297
Hey, Mr. Matlock!

377
00:26:41,366 --> 00:26:42,844
No, please come
in. What a surprise.

378
00:26:42,868 --> 00:26:44,179
Mr. Matlock, this
is Terri Young.

379
00:26:44,203 --> 00:26:46,448
Oh, a pleasure.

380
00:26:46,472 --> 00:26:49,272
I hear you've been
selling up a storm up here.

381
00:26:49,342 --> 00:26:52,075
Sun Springs is a
fabulous opportunity.

382
00:26:52,144 --> 00:26:53,722
Our homes practically
sell themselves.

383
00:26:53,746 --> 00:26:55,145
Oh, it's nice.

384
00:26:55,214 --> 00:26:57,948
There's no smog, the air's crisp

385
00:26:58,016 --> 00:26:59,783
and the drive's not bad.

386
00:26:59,852 --> 00:27:02,853
It only took me, oh...

387
00:27:02,921 --> 00:27:05,155
My watch has stopped.

388
00:27:05,224 --> 00:27:06,489
What time do you have?

389
00:27:06,559 --> 00:27:08,692
Oh, it's 11:19.

390
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:11,473
Ooh, that's one of those
digital electronic things.

391
00:27:11,497 --> 00:27:12,707
Look at all those buttons.

392
00:27:12,731 --> 00:27:16,332
So, to what do we
owe this pleasure?

393
00:27:16,402 --> 00:27:19,303
Oh, I just wanted to
see your place. Yeah.

394
00:27:19,371 --> 00:27:20,804
What time do you have?

395
00:27:21,674 --> 00:27:22,674
11:20.

396
00:27:22,708 --> 00:27:25,842
I have a friend...
He's a heart patient,

397
00:27:25,911 --> 00:27:28,912
and he sets the
alarm on his watch

398
00:27:28,981 --> 00:27:31,014
to tell him when
to take his-his pill.

399
00:27:31,083 --> 00:27:32,761
Does your watch have an alarm?

400
00:27:32,785 --> 00:27:34,952
Time, date, alarm.

401
00:27:35,020 --> 00:27:38,121
Costs $200 at
Simpson's on Wilshire.

402
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:43,160
Sun Springs.

403
00:27:43,228 --> 00:27:45,195
Terri Young speaking.

404
00:27:45,264 --> 00:27:47,197
Mr. Matlock, if you
want to look around

405
00:27:47,266 --> 00:27:48,831
on your own here,
please feel free.

406
00:27:48,900 --> 00:27:51,067
Oh, yes, I understand.

407
00:28:35,747 --> 00:28:38,860
Are you looking for
something, Mr. Matlock?

408
00:28:38,884 --> 00:28:43,954
Oh, no, no, I
just... What's this?

409
00:28:44,023 --> 00:28:46,023
Well, it's a pump.

410
00:28:46,091 --> 00:28:48,625
We had it covered to prevent
it from being tampered with.

411
00:28:48,694 --> 00:28:51,695
Sad to say, even way
out here we have vandals.

412
00:28:51,764 --> 00:28:53,263
Oh. Gee, look at that watch.

413
00:28:53,332 --> 00:28:54,898
Can I see that.

414
00:28:56,201 --> 00:28:58,179
Yes, top of the line.
It does everything

415
00:28:58,203 --> 00:28:59,035
but tap dance.

416
00:28:59,104 --> 00:29:00,370
Does it have an alarm?

417
00:29:00,439 --> 00:29:01,738
No, no, no, no, no, no.

418
00:29:01,807 --> 00:29:03,885
Watch alarms are for
people who need reminding.

419
00:29:03,909 --> 00:29:05,141
I never forget anything.

420
00:29:05,210 --> 00:29:06,510
Oh, hey.

421
00:29:10,883 --> 00:29:12,694
I was right there.

422
00:29:12,718 --> 00:29:16,686
And what did the defendant
say to the victim, Miss Young?

423
00:29:16,755 --> 00:29:19,089
He said, "Why?

424
00:29:19,158 --> 00:29:21,191
I don't understand why."

425
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:25,162
He had a very strange,
almost crazy look in his eyes.

426
00:29:25,231 --> 00:29:27,664
And by 11:00 that night,

427
00:29:27,733 --> 00:29:33,270
just three and one half hours
later, she was found dead.

428
00:29:33,338 --> 00:29:35,038
Nothing further.

429
00:29:36,275 --> 00:29:38,141
Thank you.

430
00:29:38,210 --> 00:29:41,444
Uh, Miss Young, where were you

431
00:29:41,513 --> 00:29:45,382
between 8:00 and midnight

432
00:29:45,450 --> 00:29:49,386
the night Kelly
Manning was murdered?

433
00:29:49,454 --> 00:29:51,566
Objection. The whereabouts
of this witness is irrelevant.

434
00:29:51,590 --> 00:29:52,989
The witness is not on trial.

435
00:29:53,058 --> 00:29:55,058
Your Honor, if I
might have a moment,

436
00:29:55,127 --> 00:29:56,426
my intent will become clear.

437
00:29:56,495 --> 00:29:58,195
Very well. Overruled.

438
00:29:58,263 --> 00:30:01,842
Please, uh, please
answer the question.

439
00:30:01,866 --> 00:30:04,112
On the night of the murder,

440
00:30:04,136 --> 00:30:06,214
I was at home going
over some paperwork

441
00:30:06,238 --> 00:30:08,450
with one of the partners
at Golden West...

442
00:30:08,474 --> 00:30:09,873
Mr. Davidson.

443
00:30:09,942 --> 00:30:13,143
We worked from 8:00 till
almost 2:00 in the morning.

444
00:30:13,212 --> 00:30:18,448
You were not at a concert
at Hollywood Bowl that night?

445
00:30:20,119 --> 00:30:21,384
No.

446
00:30:21,453 --> 00:30:25,889
Would you please tell the court

447
00:30:25,958 --> 00:30:30,560
who is... Chuck Carvalis?

448
00:30:32,932 --> 00:30:35,532
He's a man I date.

449
00:30:37,402 --> 00:30:41,905
He went with you to a
concert at the Hollywood Bowl

450
00:30:41,974 --> 00:30:44,774
the night Kelly
Manning was killed,

451
00:30:44,843 --> 00:30:47,277
didn't he?

452
00:30:49,748 --> 00:30:52,415
My associate...

453
00:30:52,484 --> 00:30:56,386
found this parking stub
from the Hollywood Bowl

454
00:30:56,454 --> 00:31:01,324
for that night on your car.

455
00:31:01,393 --> 00:31:05,328
Now I can call
Mr. Carvalis up here,

456
00:31:05,397 --> 00:31:09,799
but if I do, it will show

457
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:12,502
that one of you is
committing perjury.

458
00:31:12,571 --> 00:31:13,837
Do you want that?

459
00:31:18,009 --> 00:31:21,678
So were you at home
with your boss that night

460
00:31:21,747 --> 00:31:22,880
or at the concert?

461
00:31:24,683 --> 00:31:27,050
At the concert.

462
00:31:27,119 --> 00:31:29,720
Why did you lie, Miss Young?

463
00:31:31,756 --> 00:31:33,956
I lied because Steve
Davidson said he'd fire me

464
00:31:34,025 --> 00:31:36,159
if I didn't give him an alibi.

465
00:31:36,228 --> 00:31:38,172
You want to know
who killed Kelly?

466
00:31:38,196 --> 00:31:39,476
Ask him, ask Steve.

467
00:31:39,531 --> 00:31:41,998
He's the reason I lied.

468
00:31:44,236 --> 00:31:46,736
<i>I'm ashamed to admit it,</i>

469
00:31:46,805 --> 00:31:51,040
but yeah, I did, I
told Terri to lie for me.

470
00:31:51,110 --> 00:31:55,512
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

471
00:31:55,581 --> 00:31:58,415
I realized I didn't
have an alibi.

472
00:31:58,484 --> 00:31:59,549
I panicked.

473
00:31:59,618 --> 00:32:01,751
I was wrong.

474
00:32:01,819 --> 00:32:04,988
See, I was in my car, when...

475
00:32:05,056 --> 00:32:07,891
you know, Kelly was killed.

476
00:32:07,959 --> 00:32:11,728
What happened was,

477
00:32:11,797 --> 00:32:13,841
at the sales presentation
meeting that night,

478
00:32:13,865 --> 00:32:15,877
I realized that there's
some important papers

479
00:32:15,901 --> 00:32:17,301
I've left at Sun Springs.

480
00:32:17,369 --> 00:32:18,935
So I had to go back there.

481
00:32:19,003 --> 00:32:20,848
And you know
how long that takes.

482
00:32:20,872 --> 00:32:24,374
I didn't get back
till after midnight.

483
00:32:24,443 --> 00:32:26,509
And there I was, I'm alone.

484
00:32:26,578 --> 00:32:27,977
I didn't use the car phone.

485
00:32:28,046 --> 00:32:30,086
I didn't even stop
for a cup of coffee.

486
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:35,084
I bet you smoked one
of those Havana cigars

487
00:32:35,153 --> 00:32:36,586
on the way back, though.

488
00:32:36,655 --> 00:32:37,887
Yeah, probably.

489
00:32:37,956 --> 00:32:42,759
And you always use those
long wooden safety matches

490
00:32:42,828 --> 00:32:44,594
to light them, don't you?

491
00:32:44,663 --> 00:32:46,196
Yeah.

492
00:32:46,265 --> 00:32:48,731
Like, uh... Let's see...

493
00:32:48,801 --> 00:32:51,367
Like, uh, like that?

494
00:32:51,436 --> 00:32:53,737
Yeah. Yeah.

495
00:32:53,805 --> 00:32:56,005
And like, um...

496
00:32:57,943 --> 00:32:59,943
like that?

497
00:33:02,247 --> 00:33:06,082
Uh, this was found at
Kelly Manning's house

498
00:33:06,151 --> 00:33:09,219
after the murder.

499
00:33:09,287 --> 00:33:12,255
Now what would a burnt
safety match be doing

500
00:33:12,323 --> 00:33:13,689
in her wastebasket?

501
00:33:13,759 --> 00:33:16,059
I don't know. How should I know?

502
00:33:16,128 --> 00:33:19,929
You smoked a cigar at her
house that night, didn't you?

503
00:33:19,999 --> 00:33:21,375
Objection. Calls
for speculation.

504
00:33:21,399 --> 00:33:23,533
Withdraw the question.

505
00:33:23,602 --> 00:33:28,839
This match did
make me think of you.

506
00:33:28,907 --> 00:33:30,941
So I did some checking.

507
00:33:33,445 --> 00:33:35,879
Is that your signature

508
00:33:35,947 --> 00:33:38,682
on the bottom of
this credit card receipt

509
00:33:38,751 --> 00:33:41,351
from Ed's Gas Station,

510
00:33:41,420 --> 00:33:45,021
just two blocks from her house

511
00:33:45,090 --> 00:33:48,024
and dated the very
evening of the murder?

512
00:33:50,161 --> 00:33:51,828
Yeah.

513
00:33:54,933 --> 00:33:57,166
So you killed her. No!

514
00:34:00,472 --> 00:34:04,774
Okay, I-I was at
her house that night,

515
00:34:04,843 --> 00:34:07,510
but that's it, I just went
over there to find out

516
00:34:07,579 --> 00:34:10,647
why-why this guy was
walking around saying that,

517
00:34:10,716 --> 00:34:12,482
you know, she was his dead wife.

518
00:34:12,551 --> 00:34:15,685
And when you found out what
she had done seven years ago,

519
00:34:15,753 --> 00:34:17,187
you murdered her

520
00:34:17,255 --> 00:34:19,856
in an attempt to protect
Golden West Land Management.

521
00:34:19,925 --> 00:34:21,290
No! No way!

522
00:34:21,359 --> 00:34:24,372
You were angry. Yeah,
of course I was angry.

523
00:34:24,396 --> 00:34:27,330
You were very upset over what
could happen to your company.

524
00:34:27,399 --> 00:34:29,099
Yeah, of course I was upset.

525
00:34:29,167 --> 00:34:31,367
And you expect the
people in this courtroom

526
00:34:31,436 --> 00:34:33,414
to believe that Kelly
Manning was alive

527
00:34:33,438 --> 00:34:35,016
when you walked
out of her house?

528
00:34:35,040 --> 00:34:37,140
Yes, I do. They must.

529
00:34:41,313 --> 00:34:43,980
She got a phone call.

530
00:34:44,049 --> 00:34:45,548
She asked me to leave.

531
00:34:45,617 --> 00:34:47,050
I left.

532
00:34:47,118 --> 00:34:48,351
Oh, come on.

533
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:50,319
That's the truth, I swear it.

534
00:34:50,389 --> 00:34:53,589
You've lied to this court so
many times I've lost count.

535
00:34:53,658 --> 00:34:55,503
Mr. Matlock,
you've got no proof.

536
00:34:55,527 --> 00:34:57,138
And you're never
going to have any proof,

537
00:34:57,162 --> 00:34:59,196
because I did not
kill that woman.

538
00:34:59,264 --> 00:35:02,265
No further questions.

539
00:35:02,333 --> 00:35:04,701
Due to the lateness of the hour,

540
00:35:04,770 --> 00:35:07,570
this court will adjourn
until 9:00 a.m. Tuesday.

541
00:35:09,741 --> 00:35:13,409
I thought I had him.

542
00:35:13,478 --> 00:35:16,212
Hang on, Ken.
Ain't nothing easy.

543
00:35:26,858 --> 00:35:28,603
Okay, how about this?

544
00:35:29,861 --> 00:35:30,893
No.

545
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:32,195
That's not it, Tyler.

546
00:35:32,263 --> 00:35:33,974
All right, here's another one.

547
00:35:35,901 --> 00:35:38,301
Uh-uh. That's not it either.

548
00:35:38,369 --> 00:35:41,137
Wait a second.

549
00:35:41,205 --> 00:35:43,406
How about this?

550
00:35:45,343 --> 00:35:48,311
I'm afraid not, Tyler.

551
00:35:48,380 --> 00:35:51,748
You're sure none of those
were the beeps you heard?

552
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,094
Well, I'm positive.

553
00:35:53,118 --> 00:35:55,096
They're either too
low or too high or too...

554
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:56,330
I'm really sorry.

555
00:35:56,354 --> 00:35:57,420
Yeah, I'm sorry, too.

556
00:35:57,489 --> 00:35:59,656
I thought we were
onto something.

557
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:14,771
♪ ♪

558
00:36:33,592 --> 00:36:34,702
Oh! Oh!

559
00:36:34,726 --> 00:36:35,903
Excuse me! Oh, I'm sorry.

560
00:36:35,927 --> 00:36:37,160
Excuse me.

561
00:36:37,229 --> 00:36:38,528
Nice things, huh?

562
00:36:38,597 --> 00:36:40,530
Oh, yeah. Yes.

563
00:36:48,773 --> 00:36:52,041
May I help you, sir?

564
00:36:52,110 --> 00:36:54,877
Oh, yes. I'm-I'm, uh...

565
00:36:54,946 --> 00:36:56,946
I'm here for a friend.

566
00:36:57,015 --> 00:36:59,460
Of course. And what
size is your friend?

567
00:36:59,484 --> 00:37:03,986
Oh... He's about... Like that.

568
00:37:04,056 --> 00:37:06,989
Of course.

569
00:37:08,794 --> 00:37:11,138
Does he prefer a tailored look?

570
00:37:11,162 --> 00:37:13,096
Um, well... It, uh...

571
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:19,703
Or would he like something
a little more lively?

572
00:37:20,906 --> 00:37:26,275
Oh, I, um... Oh, he, um...

573
00:37:26,344 --> 00:37:29,278
He gave me this picture.

574
00:37:32,517 --> 00:37:33,817
Oh.

575
00:37:33,885 --> 00:37:36,519
I don't think I'd
have this in his size.

576
00:37:39,057 --> 00:37:41,758
Oh... It's-It's-It's not...

577
00:37:41,827 --> 00:37:44,594
It's not for him.

578
00:37:44,663 --> 00:37:48,064
He's a... It's for his girl.

579
00:37:48,133 --> 00:37:51,001
He, uh, he's got a girl.

580
00:37:51,069 --> 00:37:53,736
Well, honey, I think
that's wonderful.

581
00:37:53,805 --> 00:37:56,216
Now, I'll just show you
what's pictured here

582
00:37:56,240 --> 00:37:59,309
and some other things. You
tell me when you're moved.

583
00:37:59,377 --> 00:38:00,510
Okay.

584
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:03,279
Something like this?

585
00:38:03,348 --> 00:38:07,350
Oh, well, that's very nice.

586
00:38:10,355 --> 00:38:11,987
This?

587
00:38:12,056 --> 00:38:14,490
Oh, that's-that's nice.

588
00:38:14,559 --> 00:38:16,793
It's-It's, uh... Airy.

589
00:38:19,698 --> 00:38:21,764
Are we getting warmer?

590
00:38:21,833 --> 00:38:23,599
Oh, I say, that's, uh...

591
00:38:23,668 --> 00:38:25,935
Arlene, what do you think?

592
00:38:26,003 --> 00:38:27,437
Terrific.

593
00:38:31,242 --> 00:38:33,343
Uh...

594
00:38:33,411 --> 00:38:37,112
Uh, listen, I'm-I'm going to
go, uh, get some other stuff.

595
00:38:37,181 --> 00:38:39,749
I mean, just stuff.

596
00:38:39,818 --> 00:38:43,152
And I'll think about all this
and probably come back.

597
00:38:48,459 --> 00:38:50,371
Woops! Let met turn that off.

598
00:38:50,395 --> 00:38:52,896
Never a dull moment.

599
00:39:05,610 --> 00:39:09,579
Uh, this residential development

600
00:39:09,648 --> 00:39:14,617
out at Sun Springs that
we've talked so much about...

601
00:39:14,686 --> 00:39:17,720
it's pretty hot out there
most of the year, isn't it?

602
00:39:17,789 --> 00:39:21,824
The sun shines on Sun Springs
an average of 330 days a year.

603
00:39:21,893 --> 00:39:22,970
It's in our brochure.

604
00:39:22,994 --> 00:39:24,460
Pretty dry, too.

605
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:26,239
Yeah, it's great for
people with allergies.

606
00:39:26,263 --> 00:39:27,363
How about water?

607
00:39:27,431 --> 00:39:28,631
Water?

608
00:39:28,700 --> 00:39:29,900
Yeah, you got water out there?

609
00:39:31,035 --> 00:39:33,102
Why do you think we
call it Sun<i> Springs?</i>

610
00:39:34,439 --> 00:39:36,205
Or maybe it's because you hope

611
00:39:36,274 --> 00:39:39,108
people will believe there
is an underground spring,

612
00:39:39,177 --> 00:39:41,444
so all they have
to do is get a pump.

613
00:39:41,512 --> 00:39:43,713
But your little
irrigation system

614
00:39:43,782 --> 00:39:46,115
doesn't run by pump, does
it? It comes out of a tank.

615
00:39:46,184 --> 00:39:48,417
A tank that you have
to keep hidden away

616
00:39:48,486 --> 00:39:50,620
because it has to
constantly be filled,

617
00:39:50,688 --> 00:39:52,421
because, in truth,

618
00:39:52,490 --> 00:39:55,491
there isn't an aquifer within
30 miles of Sun Springs,

619
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:56,659
is there?

620
00:39:56,728 --> 00:39:58,039
Well, the water
will be piped in.

621
00:39:58,063 --> 00:40:01,430
At a cost so excessive
that these poor people

622
00:40:01,499 --> 00:40:03,833
you snookered into
buying lots out there

623
00:40:03,902 --> 00:40:06,268
will go broke just trying
to fill their bathtubs.

624
00:40:06,338 --> 00:40:09,071
I've never snookered anyone.

625
00:40:10,808 --> 00:40:14,778
People been taken
in like this forever,

626
00:40:14,846 --> 00:40:16,012
and Lord knows,

627
00:40:16,080 --> 00:40:18,481
plenty of useless
swamp land's been sold

628
00:40:18,550 --> 00:40:20,182
to the unsuspecting, and here

629
00:40:20,251 --> 00:40:22,685
Mr. King and his associates
have been selling desert.

630
00:40:22,754 --> 00:40:24,787
I'm talking sand, rocks,

631
00:40:24,856 --> 00:40:27,423
and no water and
no hope for water.

632
00:40:27,492 --> 00:40:29,732
Did you think suddenly
there would come a big rain

633
00:40:29,761 --> 00:40:32,728
because you're good
looking? That's stupid.

634
00:40:32,797 --> 00:40:37,233
What you planned to do was
get your money as fast as possible

635
00:40:37,301 --> 00:40:40,203
and get out of here to another
state or another country.

636
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:43,405
Unfortunately...

637
00:40:43,475 --> 00:40:46,642
a lot of people get away
with garbage like this,

638
00:40:46,711 --> 00:40:49,411
but every once in a while,
somebody gets caught.

639
00:40:49,481 --> 00:40:51,781
The system works.

640
00:40:51,850 --> 00:40:55,251
It took the death
of Kelly Manning,

641
00:40:55,319 --> 00:41:00,256
or Ann Wilson, same
person, Ken Wilson's wife.

642
00:41:00,325 --> 00:41:03,326
Your scam has been uncovered.

643
00:41:03,395 --> 00:41:04,660
It's over.

644
00:41:04,729 --> 00:41:06,529
There was no scam.

645
00:41:08,733 --> 00:41:12,801
Kelly Manning owned 50%

646
00:41:12,871 --> 00:41:17,873
rather than the usual
33.3% of Sun Springs,

647
00:41:17,942 --> 00:41:21,477
so, if anything happened to
her, you stood to gain quite a bit

648
00:41:21,546 --> 00:41:23,146
monetarily, didn't you?

649
00:41:23,214 --> 00:41:25,314
Yes, but what does that prove?

650
00:41:25,383 --> 00:41:26,949
Isn't that why first,
Steve Davidson,

651
00:41:27,018 --> 00:41:28,884
and then you, went
over there that night?

652
00:41:28,954 --> 00:41:30,286
No.

653
00:41:30,355 --> 00:41:32,422
You knew my
client was distraught.

654
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:33,656
Almost out of control.

655
00:41:33,724 --> 00:41:35,525
You knew he broke
into her house.

656
00:41:35,593 --> 00:41:38,261
And probably his fingerprints
were all over the place.

657
00:41:38,329 --> 00:41:41,230
I-I... Didn't you
kill Kelly Manning,

658
00:41:41,299 --> 00:41:43,633
so that your scam would
never be uncovered?

659
00:41:43,701 --> 00:41:46,569
And Ken Wilson, being an
ex-con, was the perfect patsy?

660
00:41:46,637 --> 00:41:48,403
Objection.

661
00:41:48,473 --> 00:41:50,773
Mr. Matlock is not only
badgering the witness,

662
00:41:50,842 --> 00:41:52,619
he is engaging in
rampant speculation.

663
00:41:52,643 --> 00:41:54,010
Sustained.

664
00:41:54,079 --> 00:41:56,779
This line of questioning,
if you can even call it that,

665
00:41:56,848 --> 00:41:58,147
is unacceptable, Counselor.

666
00:41:58,216 --> 00:41:59,849
Yes, Sir.

667
00:41:59,918 --> 00:42:02,285
Uh, how about this?

668
00:42:02,353 --> 00:42:04,754
Miss Manning's
next-door neighbor

669
00:42:04,823 --> 00:42:09,258
Estelle Metzger testified that
at approximately 11:00 pm,

670
00:42:09,327 --> 00:42:11,326
she heard Miss Manning scream,

671
00:42:11,395 --> 00:42:15,565
entered her house,
heard two strange beeps,

672
00:42:15,634 --> 00:42:17,700
heard someone go
out the back door,

673
00:42:17,769 --> 00:42:20,302
discovered Miss
Manning's dead body.

674
00:42:20,371 --> 00:42:23,573
Where were you at
approximately 11:00 pm?

675
00:42:23,641 --> 00:42:25,174
At home.

676
00:42:25,242 --> 00:42:26,854
Where was your
car? In the garage.

677
00:42:26,878 --> 00:42:28,311
Are you certain?

678
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:30,379
Absolutely.

679
00:42:30,448 --> 00:42:36,185
At... 10:42 that night,

680
00:42:36,254 --> 00:42:39,855
a call was placed from your car

681
00:42:39,924 --> 00:42:41,557
to Miss Manning's house.

682
00:42:43,661 --> 00:42:47,397
Your Honor, by
previous stipulation,

683
00:42:47,465 --> 00:42:49,532
with the people, I offer

684
00:42:49,601 --> 00:42:54,404
what purports to be Mr. King's
cellular car telephone bill

685
00:42:54,472 --> 00:42:56,149
including the
night of the murder

686
00:42:56,173 --> 00:42:58,619
and ask that it be marked
Defendant Exhibit "F."

687
00:42:58,643 --> 00:43:00,676
It shall be marked.

688
00:43:00,745 --> 00:43:02,611
Okay.

689
00:43:02,680 --> 00:43:05,581
That is your number
and your bill, isn't it?

690
00:43:05,650 --> 00:43:07,216
Well, it appears to be.

691
00:43:07,285 --> 00:43:13,155
Yeah, and 555-8725 is or was
Kelly Manning's phone number,

692
00:43:13,224 --> 00:43:15,291
wasn't it? Yes.

693
00:43:15,359 --> 00:43:17,826
So, you were not
at home that night.

694
00:43:17,895 --> 00:43:19,295
You were in your car.

695
00:43:19,364 --> 00:43:22,598
In fact, it was you who called
while Mr. Davidson was there.

696
00:43:22,667 --> 00:43:23,800
Yes.

697
00:43:23,868 --> 00:43:25,334
Why did you call her that night?

698
00:43:25,403 --> 00:43:26,736
I don't remember.

699
00:43:26,805 --> 00:43:28,615
Let me see if I
can fill in the gaps.

700
00:43:28,639 --> 00:43:32,975
You drove over to her house,

701
00:43:33,044 --> 00:43:35,544
saw Steve Davidson's car there,

702
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:37,180
called her, told
her to get rid of him.

703
00:43:37,248 --> 00:43:39,515
Said you needed
to talk with her alone,

704
00:43:39,584 --> 00:43:41,495
but actually, you
intended to kill her,

705
00:43:41,519 --> 00:43:42,618
which you did.

706
00:43:42,687 --> 00:43:43,931
That is not true!

707
00:43:45,056 --> 00:43:46,355
What's that?

708
00:43:46,424 --> 00:43:47,668
Miss Metzger, is that
the sound you heard?

709
00:43:47,692 --> 00:43:49,759
That's it! That's it!

710
00:43:49,828 --> 00:43:50,971
Those are the beeps
I heard that night!

711
00:43:50,995 --> 00:43:52,094
Those are the beeps?

712
00:43:52,163 --> 00:43:54,764
Thank you, Miss Metzger.

713
00:43:54,833 --> 00:43:56,544
Those beeps seemed to
be coming from your pocket.

714
00:43:56,568 --> 00:43:59,869
Could we see what's making them?

715
00:43:59,938 --> 00:44:01,537
It's my pager.

716
00:44:01,606 --> 00:44:05,508
Oh. Mmm.

717
00:44:06,811 --> 00:44:12,715
I heard one of these
the other day at a place.

718
00:44:12,784 --> 00:44:16,118
Do you have a
service that beeps you

719
00:44:16,186 --> 00:44:20,122
whenever someone calls
you or leaves a message,

720
00:44:20,190 --> 00:44:23,325
as my associate just did?

721
00:44:23,395 --> 00:44:25,294
Yes, that's right.

722
00:44:25,363 --> 00:44:28,897
So, if what Miss
Metzger said is true,

723
00:44:28,966 --> 00:44:33,803
and the beeps she
heard came from this,

724
00:44:33,871 --> 00:44:39,442
then that must mean
you are the murderer.

725
00:44:39,510 --> 00:44:43,445
No, as you said, a lot of
people carry those beepers.

726
00:44:43,514 --> 00:44:46,048
It's simply a coincidence.

727
00:44:46,117 --> 00:44:48,050
Hmm.

728
00:44:48,119 --> 00:44:49,585
Ordinarily, I would
agree with that.

729
00:44:49,654 --> 00:44:54,523
Except for this one last detail.

730
00:44:57,595 --> 00:45:00,630
This is a copy of the record

731
00:45:00,698 --> 00:45:03,298
your answering service
provided me with.

732
00:45:03,367 --> 00:45:05,735
And do you know what happened

733
00:45:05,803 --> 00:45:08,771
at approximately 11:00
pm the night of the murder?

734
00:45:08,840 --> 00:45:09,939
That's right.

735
00:45:10,008 --> 00:45:12,708
They paged you on your beeper.

736
00:45:12,777 --> 00:45:15,945
Now, how did I know
that you weren't home

737
00:45:16,013 --> 00:45:17,113
when they paged you?

738
00:45:17,182 --> 00:45:22,852
Because you
responded to that page

739
00:45:22,920 --> 00:45:27,422
by calling your
answering service at 11:05

740
00:45:27,491 --> 00:45:29,659
from the phone in your car.

741
00:45:34,298 --> 00:45:36,365
Mr. King, I have
to tell you the truth.

742
00:45:36,434 --> 00:45:40,369
I don't believe
that's a coincidence.

743
00:45:46,043 --> 00:45:49,311
We, the jury, find the
defendant not guilty.

744
00:45:49,380 --> 00:45:51,780
Thank you, ladies and
gentlemen of the jury.

745
00:45:51,849 --> 00:45:53,129
You're dismissed.

746
00:45:53,183 --> 00:45:54,461
And this court is adjourned.

747
00:45:55,686 --> 00:45:56,930
I can't thank you enough.

748
00:45:56,954 --> 00:45:58,114
Second time's the charm, son.

749
00:45:58,155 --> 00:46:00,322
Let's go home.

750
00:46:11,102 --> 00:46:16,372
Oh, my, it is so wonderful
to be 40... something.

751
00:46:24,215 --> 00:46:25,515
The party's almost over!

752
00:46:25,583 --> 00:46:26,794
Plane just got here.

753
00:46:26,818 --> 00:46:28,250
Did you get her something hot?

754
00:46:30,488 --> 00:46:36,158
Bernice... Oh, thank
you, Lester, dear!

755
00:46:36,227 --> 00:46:40,963
Oh... What is it?

756
00:46:41,032 --> 00:46:44,567
Chester Taft got her a
digital watch with a moon on it.

757
00:46:44,636 --> 00:46:46,301
Oh.

758
00:46:46,370 --> 00:46:49,038
Oh, how sweet.

759
00:46:49,106 --> 00:46:51,040
With all the little buttons.

760
00:46:54,345 --> 00:46:55,645
Oh!

761
00:46:58,016 --> 00:47:00,516
You devil!

762
00:47:00,585 --> 00:47:01,817
Oh, you devil.

763
00:47:05,490 --> 00:47:08,050
That is hilarious. Look at that.

